Use setjmp() with libpng's jmp_buf on zedBSD.

The PNG loader saves libpng's error context with sigsetjmp() on
png_jmpbuf(png), which is a jmp_buf.  That works where sigjmp_buf and
jmp_buf are the same type (glibc); on zedBSD sigjmp_buf is a different
structure and the call does not compile.  libpng leaves its context with
longjmp(), so setjmp() is the matching call; on zedBSD the loader now
uses it, as it already does where sigsetjmp() is absent.  Other systems
are unchanged.

--- a/gdk/loaders/gdkpng.c
+++ b/gdk/loaders/gdkpng.c
@@ -37,8 +37,13 @@
 
 /* {{{ Callbacks */
 
-/* No sigsetjmp on Windows */
-#ifndef HAVE_SIGSETJMP
+/* No sigsetjmp on Windows.  On zedBSD sigjmp_buf is not jmp_buf, and
+ * png_jmpbuf() is a jmp_buf that libpng leaves with longjmp(), so setjmp()
+ * is the call that matches it. */
+#if !defined(HAVE_SIGSETJMP) || defined(__ZEDBSD__)
+#undef sigjmp_buf
+#undef sigsetjmp
+#undef siglongjmp
 #define sigjmp_buf jmp_buf
 #define sigsetjmp(jb, x) setjmp(jb)
 #define siglongjmp longjmp
